From: Poco F1 iOS port
Subject: [PATCH] Poco F1: the system cache, DDR and L3 tuning of 3009

The Mi 8's patch 3009 only ran on the Mi 8, but nothing in it depends on that phone: LLCC and the L3 and DDR votes are the
SoC's. Mi 8 notes: the Poco F1 "has the same gate and the same missing LLCC and votes". sweetmemtune=0 still turns it off.
sweet_board_beryllium() is true on both phones (the Mi 8's ADT also lists xiaomi,beryllium).

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
@@ -1001,7 +1001,7 @@
 {
 	int on = 1;
 	(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetmemtune", &on, sizeof(on));
-	if (!on || !sweet_board_is("xiaomi,dipper")) {
+	if (!on || !sweet_board_beryllium()) {
 		return;
 	}
 	if (__atomic_exchange_n(&sweet_mem_lock, 1, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE) == 0) {
